  "fails_if": "`compile_coding_register` stops comparing a `[[coding.choice]]` entry's expected_evidence_sha256 with the evidence of the delivery it builds, so the VALUE choice reviewed over the two pooled blank rows and the 2013 donor still applies after the column gains a 2014 peer",
  "note": "The replaced test's drift leg: VALUE gains a later physical peer (CVID 2104) after the choice was reviewed over the errata-pooled blanks (CVIDs 2101, 2102) and the donor (2103), so the choice goes stale and the 2010 conflict comes back. The compiled guard reported peer_membership_changed; at the boundary the build reports a stale_curation_entry for the choice's period. The choice's evidence digest covers its column's own originals and bound lists, so the new peer is what stales it; it is the fresh-build form of the drift the deleted test asserted on a stored case. Only pooled.toml is committed, so no other register's entry can mask the claim. The replaced twocols leg (adding an A peer stales only the A choice while B still applies) is step 3. The [[errata.delivered]] entry was re-reviewed over the new VALUE peer, so its evidence pin reads the built delivery (`read=built`); only the choice keeps the reviewed delivery's digest.",
